{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-06-07T13:11:22Z","updated_at":"2020-06-07T13:11:22Z","body":"I run into the same problem on Fedora and a fresh Ubuntu-VM\r\n\r\nI couldn't follow your suggestions with appending the runtime. I just uncommented the existing cat command in `build_appimage` and made sure the runtime-File is in that folder beforehand. \r\n\r\n`wget -q -O runtime https://github.com/AppImage/AppImageKit/releases/download/continuous/runtime-x86_64`\r\n`cat runtime >> app.AppImage`\r\n\r\nBut I then get `execv error: No such file or directory` when trying to run the AppImage\r\n\r\nCould you explain your solution a bit more precisely?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/comments/640216725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"lucaheise","id":19505247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NTA1MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19505247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise","html_url":"https://github.com/lucaheise","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucaheise/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/comments/641177973","html_url":"https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/601#issuecomment-641177973","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/601","id":641177973,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY0MTE3Nzk3Mw==","user":{"login":"alvarohm","id":4748897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NDg4OTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4748897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm","html_url":"https://github.com/alvarohm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alvarohm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-06-09T09:55:22Z","updated_at":"2020-06-09T09:55:22Z","body":"Hi. There were a few more problems in the script `build_appimage` that I had forgotten to mention in my post. I fixed them first and then started focusing on the AppImage runtime, so I forgot about the other problems. Apologies for the omission. Here's a rundown of the issue I have found and a version of the script that works for me. I hope this helps.\r\n\r\n1) The script is in the `appimage` folder, so the `deb` folder is below `appimage`, not inside `bundle`.\r\n2) Before copying `app` and the icon to `app.AppDir`, we need to `cd` into `app.AppDir` as the folder `usr` has already been copied.\r\n3) The path to the icon has a type in `256x265`, it should be `256x256`.\r\n4) We need to `cd` back to `appimage` before creating and copying the `.desktop` file to created it in appimage. \r\n5) The appimage should not be redirected into `app.AppImage` not appended. Appending it only works if the file was empty or did not exist before.\r\n\r\nWith this changes (including the download of the runtime), the script builds an AppImage that works for me. Note that if you run `yarn tauri:build`, the script is reverted back. \r\n\r\nHere's the full script that worked for me:\r\n\r\n```\r\n#!/bin/bash\r\n\r\nmkdir -p app.AppDir\r\ncp -r ../deb/app_0.1.0_amd64/data/usr app.AppDir\r\n\r\ncd app.AppDir\r\n\r\ncp usr/bin/app AppRun\r\ncp usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/app.png app.png\r\n\r\ncd ..\r\n\r\necho '[Desktop Entry]' > app.desktop\r\necho 'Version=1.0' >> app.desktop\r\necho 'Comment=A Tauri App' >> app.desktop\r\necho 'Exec=app' >> app.desktop\r\necho 'Icon=app' >> app.desktop\r\necho 'Name=APP' >> app.desktop\r\necho 'Terminal=false' >> app.desktop\r\necho 'Type=Application' >> app.desktop\r\necho 'Categories=X-Web;' >> app.desktop\r\n\r\ncp app.desktop app.AppDir/usr/share/applications/app.desktop\r\n\r\n\r\nmksquashfs app.AppDir app.squashfs -root-owned -noappend\r\n\r\nwget -q -O runtime https://github.com/AppImage/AppImageKit/releases/download/continuous/runtime-x86_64\r\ncat runtime > app.AppImage\r\n# cat runtime >> app.AppImage\r\ncat app.squashfs >> app.AppImage\r\nchmod a+x app.AppImage\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tauri-apps/tauri/issues/comments/641177973/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,